Measured correction recorded, not hidden
-----------------------------------------
1. The registry pin for os-preview-writer-census read 63 while the suite it
   names already ran 67, so the previous round's claimed bump was not on disk.
   This round writes the measured 71.
2. The index/chain order is a fixed point, not a one-way order: chain quotes
   index.html's byte size in its back-hop block, so writing chain then index
   makes chain stale (56337 vs 56466) and writing index then chain leaves the
   index band without the caveat. Iterating chain -> index -> chain -> index
   converges once index bytes stop moving (56466 both passes), and only then
   do both pages read PASS.

